Just FYI - there are existing packages that will model based on groups. For example:

library(lme4)

## Using data from Brandon's example
> ans <- lmList(yvar ~ xvar | Site_id, data = datatst)
> dd <- summary(ans)
> cbind(coef(ans), dd$r.squared)
  (Intercept)      xvar dd$r.squared
A   -5.078472 1.0142138    0.9910703
B   -1.641414 0.9549062    0.9847991

Matt

