Are you concerned about the fate of federally funded datasets?

See the call below (and attached pdf… same info, maybe better formatting) for more information and details about the DataRescue event this coming Thursday.  Note that experience is NOT necessary nor do you have to stay the whole time.

Please forward widely.

===

DataRescue UC Davis – Call to Action

Join us for #DataRescueDavis, where we will work together to backup climate and environmental research and data currently available through federal websites that are at risk of disappearing under the current federal administration.

Date/Time: Thursday, February 2nd, 10 AM to 4 PM (come when you can)

Location: Shields Library, room 360 (the DSI classroom, 3rd floor)

Up-to-date information:  http://guides.lib.ucdavis.edu/aiap_events

Bring: laptops
Who should attend: Anyone interested in ensuring that scientific data are not lost because of political change.

—Free food, coffee, etc. provided throughout the day—

—Experience not required; training provided during the first hour—

Activities:

1)     Seeding the End of Term web crawler with priority URLs (training provided)

2)     Hackathon: Scraping and downloading vulnerable datasets (should know a scripting language, such as R or Python, or be able to detect patterns in HTML. Overview of scraping techniques provided during first hour.)

Contact:  datares...@gmail.com

Hosted by the UC Davis Library and the Data Science Initiative in collaboration with #DataRefuge, the EDGI, the Internet Archive’s End of Term 2016 project to archive the federal webpages and data that are in danger of disappearing during the current federal administration. Our event focuses on preserving information and data at high risk of being removed from online public access or even deleted.

Michele Tobias, PhD

GIS Data Curator

Data Management Program

UC Davis Library

161 Shields Library

(530)752-7532

mmto...@ucdavis.edu

